-- title:
--   Proj Sub Meas Sandwich Sum Le One
-- statement:
--   **A bounded middle operator sandwiched by a projective submeasurement sums to at most one.**
--
--   Let `A` be a finite projective submeasurement and let `B` be an operator satisfying $B\le1$. Then the sum of all outcome sandwiches is bounded by the identity:
--
--   $$
--   \sum_a A_a\,B\,A_a\le1.
--   $$
--
--   The inequality is in the operator order. It is the contraction estimate used repeatedly in the switcheroo fourth-term chain, where `B` is a complete-part total or another positive operator bounded by one.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.projSubMeas_sandwich_sum_le_one`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
